# DK0: the drafter selector's plumbing control: the production profile plus QWEN_FAST_DRAFTER_CHECKPOINT naming the DEFAULT checkpoint. READ: the "[PINDIAG] drafter checkpoint id=dflash2-dedf8df6 ... verified=default" line (the default carries no pins, so this proves the selector path ran and nothing about the bytes), the answers' hashes equal S0-CTL's
# (the selector path changes no byte). A candidate arm is only credible after this one passes. No candidate id exists yet: Dk-<id> templates are made from D1/D2 when a candidate's pins are committed (README).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the combined development window (docs/tp4-combined-window.md; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w2-levern-prefix and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the classes, the minutes, the NEEDS graph, the swap
# rules and every read and cutover rule. ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed branch commit; every window job serves it. The jobs named
# CTL (and T0, G0, E1-CTL) run the PRODUCTION base image tp4-serve-10 (the production engine bytes), driven from this same window commit: the host-side scripts (the smoke shapes, the gates, the kill-switch preflight, the load logger, the raised exactness-shared box) are the window's.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w2ln-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-dckdefault
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
